# Contact form email delivery (src/components/ContactForm.tsx)
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same variable in your
# host's environment (Vercel: Project Settings -> Environment Variables), then
# redeploy. Without it the form shows an error instead of silently pretending
# the request was delivered.
#
# To get a key: go to https://web3forms.com, enter
# Gtech.distribution@outlook.com, and the access key is emailed to you.
# No account or password is created. Quote requests are delivered to whichever
# address the key was issued to, so there is no recipient to configure here.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is required, and correct: the form submits from the visitor's
# browser because Web3Forms rejects server-to-server calls on the free plan.
# The key is public by design and only allows sending mail TO that inbox.
# Changing it requires a rebuild, since Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_ values.

NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
